This project adapts Shipyard (https://github.com/vineethvarghese/shipyard, MIT License), a Claude Code plugin,
for GitHub Copilot: Copilot CLI, the Copilot coding agent and Copilot agent mode in IDEs. The agents, skills,
registry, contracts, scripts, hooks and workflows are ported from Shipyard; the credits Shipyard records in its
own NOTICE apply here in full:

1. Elephant/goldfish method
   https://github.com/vshvedov/elephant-goldfish — MIT License.
   The P2 brainstorm and the cold readiness check of each slice spec are adapted from this method.

2. Grilling, domain-modelling, specification and TDD skills
   https://github.com/mattpocock/skills — MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock.
   The P4 grill, the inline glossary and the three-part decision test, the user-story and seams-under-test
   sections of the spec, and the seam-first test discipline are adapted from these skills.

3. "Cranky Old Sam" reviewer persona — MIT License.
   The simplicity reviewer's voice is adapted from this persona.

4. Contributed review profiles: the code reviewer and the security reviewer are adapted from contributed
   review agents.

5. Books — ideas paraphrased, never quoted: Ousterhout (A Philosophy of Software Design), Gregg (Systems
   Performance), Evans (Domain-Driven Design).

6. Inspiration: Akash Singhal (https://github.com/akashsinghal).

